Spec: Plugin Update Command

Purpose:
  Refresh managed plugins using their recorded versions or a requested version for one repository-qualified plugin.

Owns:
  ./update.ts
  ./update.test.ts

References:
  /src/services/plugin-updater/plugin-updater.sdd

Must:
  Receive a @PluginUpdateCommandContainer providing @PluginUpdater.update.
  Return an `update` command for attachment beneath the `plugin` group.
  Expose `specdd plugin update [repository] [pluginname] [version]`.
  Describe the optional version in help as a branch, tag, or commit reachable from a branch or tag.
  Require repository and plugin name together for a targeted update; accept no arguments to update all managed plugins.
  Reject a lone repository or bare plugin name before invoking the service.
  Accept the same repository syntax as `plugin add`: GitHub shorthand, SSH addresses, and HTTPS URLs.
  Forward the absolute current working directory, optional repository, optional plugin name, and optional version to @PluginUpdater.update.
  Preserve omitted arguments as absent so the service can select all plugins or retain a recorded version.
  Reject extra positional arguments and unknown options before invoking the service.

Must not:
  Read registry files, select registrations, resolve versions, or perform installations directly.

Exposes:
  @createPluginUpdateCommand
  @PluginUpdateCommandContainer

Scenario: all plugins
  When `specdd plugin update` runs
  Then @PluginUpdater.update receives no repository, plugin name, or version override

Scenario: one plugin at a new version
  When `specdd plugin update \@acme/plugins review v2.0.0` runs
  Then @PluginUpdater.update receives repository `\@acme/plugins`, plugin name `review`, and version `v2.0.0`
